char RAWSTR_chsrc_USAGE_ENGLISH[] = "NAME:\012   chsrc - Change Source - (GPLv3+)\012\012VERSION:\012   @ver@\012\012USAGE:\012   chsrc <command> [options] [dish] [mirror]\012\012COMMANDS:\012   help,  h                 Print this help, or -h, --help\012   issue, i                 See related issues\012\012   list, ls, l              List available mirror sites and supported dishes\012   list  mirror|dish        List supported:  mirror sites/supported dishes\012   list  os|lang|ware       List supported: OSes/Programming Languages/Softwares\012   list   <dish>            View available sources and supporting features for <dish>\012\012   measure, m, cesu <dish>  Measure velocity of all sources of <dish>\012\012   get, g <dish>            View the current source state for <dish>\012\012   set, s <dish>            Change source, select the fastest source by automatic speed measurement\012   set    <dish>  first     Change source, select the fastest source measured by the maintainers team\012   set    <dish> <mirror>   Change source, specify a mirror site (Via `list <dish>`)\012   set    <dish>  <URL>     Change source, using user-defined source URL\012   reset  <dish>            Reset  source to the upstream's default\012\012   scan                     Read-only detection of manageable sources on this machine\012   plan                     Build a setup plan (read-only)\012   setup                    Scan and apply; user-level automatic items only by default\012\012OPTIONS:\012   -dry                       Dry Run. Simulate the source changing process, command only prints, not run\012   -scope=project|user|system Change source only for this project / user level / system level (Via `ls <dish>`)\012   -ipv6                      Speed measurement using IPv6\012   -en(glish)                 Output in English\012   -no-color                  Output without color\012\012MAINTAIN:\012   chsrc respects contributors. We even have the \042Contributor_t\042 struct. All the info of\012   them flows into runtime, and will never be erased by the compiler merely as comments.\012\012   chsrc is interesting. The \042restaurant metaphor\042 runs through the entire program. chsrc\012   acts as a \042waiter\042, accepting users' requests (get, set, ls) for a certain \042dish\042. The\012   kitchen \042prepare\042s the ingredients as needed. The \042chef\042 and the \042saucier\042 follow the\012   \042recipe\042 to serve the dish. Changing \042source\042s means changing the \042provider\042 of the\012   ingredients for that dish.\012\012   Source Code: https://github.com/RubyMetric/chsrc";

